## Development

Requires a C++{{ cpp_standard }} compiler (GCC or Clang), CMake 3.25+, Ninja,
clang-format, clang-tidy and [just](https://just.systems/); gcovr, Doxygen,
clangd, prek and ccache are used when present. `just doctor` reports what is
missing and how to install it.

```sh
just setup   # configure the dev build, install git hooks
just check   # format check, clang-tidy, build and tests
just         # list every recipe
```

| Task | Tool |
| --- | --- |
| Build | CMake presets, Ninja, ccache |
| Dependencies | CPM.cmake |
| Format and lint | clang-format, clang-tidy (warnings are errors) |
| Tests | Catch2 v3 through CTest, ASan + UBSan preset |
| Coverage | gcovr |
| Docs | Doxygen |
| Git hooks | prek |

Dependencies are downloaded and built from source by CPM.cmake. To let a
package manager (Conan, vcpkg, system packages) supply them instead, configure
with `-DCPM_USE_LOCAL_PACKAGES=ON`: every `CPMAddPackage` then tries
`find_package()` first.

The layout follows [pitchfork](https://github.com/vector-of-bool/pitchfork):
public headers in `include/`, sources in `src/`, plus `tests/`, `examples/`
and `docs/`.

The repository carries Claude Code settings (`CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/`): edits
are auto-formatted, `just check` runs before Claude finishes a task, and the
`clangd-lsp` plugin provides the language server.
